The following command is all that is required to enable building umr on a fresh
CentOS 8 install (after an initial "yum -y update"):

yum --enablerepo=PowerTools  install cmake automake autoconf libdrm-devel llvm-devel llvm-static libpciaccess* ncurses-devel zlib-devel libdrm-devel vim gcc gcc-c++ gdb strace make 

(note strace/gdb/vim aren't strictly necessary but I tend to install those reflexively ...)


